>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Xiaolong</forename><surname>Michael Y Fatemi</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Zora</forename><forename type=\"middle\">Zhiruo</forename><surname>Jin</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Apurva</forename><surname>Wang</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Yueqi</forename><surname>Gandhi</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Yu</forename><surname>Song</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Jayanth</forename><surname>Gu</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Gaowen</forename><surname>Srinivasa</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Graham</forename><surname>Liu</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Neubig</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<idno type=\"arXiv\">arXiv:2504.07079</idno>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">Web agents can self-improve by discovering and honing skills</title>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2025\">2025</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note type=\"report_type\">arXiv preprint</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b38\">\n\t<analytic>\n\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">A APPENDIX A.1 ANALYSIS Tools. In Figure 6, we include a list of all tools discovered across the WebArena and VisualWe-bArena benchmarks, as well as the number of attempts required to obtain a validated implementation. As seen, most tools are discovered on the first attempt, but a few more nuanced functionalities</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Shuyan</forename><surname>Zhou</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Frank</forename><forename type=\"middle\">F</forename><surname>Xu</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Hao</forename><surname>Zhu</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Xuhui</forename><surname>Zhou</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Robert</forename><surname>Lo</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Abishek</forename><surname>Sridhar</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Xianyi</forename><surname>Cheng</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Tianyue</forename><surname>Ou</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Yonatan</forename><surname>Bisk</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Daniel</forename><surname>Fried</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t</analytic>\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\">The Twelfth International Conference on Learning Representations</title>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2024\">2024</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>Webarena: A realistic web environment for building autonomous agents require as many as 4 attempts</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b39\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">In Figure 8a, we include additional fine-grained performance analysis of our method on the Classifieds benchmark. First, we analyze the frequency and average length of successful and failed trajectories, segmented by the agent&apos;s own assessment of the task outcome -as found in concurrent work</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">;</forename><surname>Performance</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><surname>Andrade</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2025\">2025</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n\t<note>web agents suffer from an &quot;agreement bias&quot; and frequently rationalize even failed trajectories as successful Our approach mitigates this bias by using an external verifier to corroborate the agent&apos;s assessment</note>\n</biblStruct>\n\n\t\t\t\t</listBibl>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</back>\n\t</text>\n</TEI>\n","pdf_hash":"f2688fa55021641f556839cdb01a943cccd836f08a03ee8bdd468cb3ec4db630","tables":[{"table_id":"tab_0","section_path_id":"1~15","section_ordinal":25,"caption":"Table 2 :","coordinates":null,"cells":[{"row":0,"column":0,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"browser LLM","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":176,"end":187},"digest":"da961fd7df26583f30c2dff9c412494a04212856d380751a623e70caf094edca"},{"row":0,"column":1,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"tools","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":187,"end":192},"digest":"0ea0d6351830e347a643ba35361708764a78dc6b37b7312f670c1b7ff869c5f8"},{"row":0,"column":2,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"dom-parser","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":192,"end":202},"digest":"0f255ccc5b9149153bca7cf49f529f464533bd596b55398861a65c3c71c234c8"},{"row":0,"column":3,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"verify","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":202,"end":208},"digest":"20e8f8452ced1e7aba2353022b9eeddec016b264726edee9790593717e3c04e4"},{"row":0,"column":4,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"avg #steps (↓)","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":208,"end":222},"digest":"3204b12738aa58e8b6406dfdcb09df3ef54a23bc4dee19b30cefef2de15241fb"},{"row":0,"column":5,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"SR (%) ↑","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":222,"end":230},"digest":"497676dd8cefcba2c943afa73ab7347b03c37f68e391e70ce8152d86b9e21aad"},{"row":1,"column":0,"colspan":1,"rowspan":1,"text":"gpt-4.1","coordinates":null,"span":{"start":230,"end":237},"digest":"87a890